 379: # ---- the TIME label: an accepted read returns the value of the PREVIOUS update, then updates -- so a refused access
 380: #  that reached crime_update_crime_time() would show in the NEXT read.  The first `ld' latches last_microseconds; on the
 381: #  fixed build the next `ld' reads what the device tick added (measured 66 or 132), far below SMALL (0.1 s of TIME);
 382: #  a fall-through at 0x38 makes it the wall-clock interval of the intervening debugger commands, ~1e8.  The third `ld'
 383: #  is the CONTROL that the channel moves.  (Opus pass 2, E3.)
 384: SMALL = 66 * 100000
